flour is hardly flammable.

> IIRC, flour and sugar and
> things like that explode if they are packed together,

That would be new to me. But I seem to recall an experiment where sugar
mixed with ash can be set on fire, while sugar alone won't burn.

There are things, though, that explode easily if put together. Examples
are glycerine and potassium permanganate which will catch fire, or sugar
with an extreem oxidant like perchlorates. There are other substances,
e.g. those used in rockets, hydracine may catch fire/explode on contact
with oxidants.

